# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the example, not the real one.
#
# WARNING: anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the client bundle and is readable by anyone
# who opens the page. Acceptable for a laptop at a booth. NOT safe for a hosted deployment --
# and this repo already publishes to GitHub Pages, so a key added here reaches the internet.
# Route model calls through a server-side relay before any key goes near a deployed build.

# ElevenLabs is optional. With no key the chef speaks through the browser and nothing else
# changes.
VITE_ELEVENLABS_KEY=
VITE_ELEVENLABS_VOICE=

# OpenAI: the counter scan, the "what am I missing" answer, and the end-of-session debrief.
# With no key those three degrade to the local fault text, which is already a complete sentence.
VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Model ids change often; check the current list rather than trusting a default.
# VITE_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini

# The recipe-book and leaderboard API (server/). Read at BUILD time, so a change needs a
# rebuild. This is a public URL, not a secret -- unlike the keys above, it is safe to inline.
#
# Unset, the app still works: the recipe book falls back to the recipes bundled in
# src/core/recipe.ts and the leaderboard shows the local booth board only.
# VITE_API_URL=https://is-it-done-yet-api.onrender.com
VITE_API_URL=
